-## Known risk: J604 SD reader port
-
-`pcie_prepare_fdt()` powers each enabled T8132 port that carries `pwren-gpios`,
-and accepts only the gP13 radio rail. If the J604 kernel DT gives the SD reader
-port a `pwren-gpios` (gP19), preparation fails, and kboot disables every
-`apple,t8132-pcie` host: the radio and the SD reader together. That is fail
-closed, but costs Wi-Fi. Either the kernel DT leaves the SD reader rail to
-Linux, or the SD rail gets its own source-verified entry. Both are kernel-side
-decisions, out of scope here.
+## J604 SD reader port
+
+The J604 apcie has a second root port, pci-bridge2, with the SD reader
+(pcie-sdreader). Its rail is ADT `function-sd_pwr_en` = SMC GPIO `gP19`,
+action `pKW4`, template 0: a plain SMC GPIO output, the same type as the
+M4 Pro J614s `sd_pwr_en` (gP19, template 0). The kernel DT describes it as
+`pwren-gpios` on that port, as the t600x/t602x SD reader ports do, and
+pcie-apple drives it before it trains the port. `pcie_prepare_fdt()` leaves
+such a rail to the OS (no SMC write, no DART bypass) after checking in the
+ADT that every pKW4 function of that line is a plain output of the SMC PMU;
+it still prepares only the qualified gP13 radio action, and refuses any rail
+the ADT does not describe that way.
